# What GitHub puts in the release tarball — i.e. what lands in a customer's folder.
# The install is `curl .../<tag>.tar.gz | tar -xz --strip-components=1`, so anything
# tracked here is copied verbatim into their AIOS root. LICENSE and README.md exist
# for the PUBLIC REPO (a client's AI refused an install over a repo with no public
# identity — c8cb44d, 2026-08-21); they are repo furniture, not part of the product
# folder, and they were landing in every customer's root as clutter nothing points at.
# `export-ignore` keeps them on github.com and out of the tarball.
# Anchored to the root on purpose: api/template.js in the engine skips these by exact
# root-relative path, and the two rules must describe the same thing.
/LICENSE        export-ignore
/README.md      export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
# `.gitignore` is NOT export-ignored since 0.9.0 (D34): every customer folder gets it, so
# `system/.secrets/` (API keys), `.aios-license` and `.mcp.json` never reach git even if the
# customer later makes the folder a repo. api/template.js ships it on the manifest route too.
# CI of this repo: not part of the product folder.
/.github        export-ignore
